<title>USA: GM strike idles 7,478 U.S., Mexican workers.</title>
<headline>GM strike idles 7,478 U.S., Mexican workers.</headline>
<dateline>WARREN, Mich. 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp said Friday afternoon 7,478 U.S. and Mexican workers have been idled by the work stoppage in Canada.</p>
<p>That figure was unchanged from Friday morning, the world's largest automaker said.</p>
<p>There will be no change in the status of operations over the weekend, GM said in a news release.</p>
<p>The strike began October 3.</p>
<p>GM stock closed unchanged at 53-1/4 on the New York Stock Exchange Friday.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
